{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Phase 2 — fix pushed for review: Gerrit change 2336\n\n`https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2336` — \"Bound the MCP list read surface\".\nNOT submitted; `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1` still pending.\n\n### What changed\n\n**1. The list surface is now BOUNDED, and refuses rather than truncates.**\n`src/rebar/_mcp_budget.py` (new) holds the payload-budget cluster lifted out of\n`mcp_server.py` — a real call-graph seam: both bounds measure through `_payload_bytes`,\nand `mcp_server.py` had reached the 800-LOC hard cap. Alongside the existing\n`_cap_workflow_payload` it adds `_bound_list_payload`, which reuses the SAME\n`_WORKFLOW_TOKEN_BUDGET_BYTES` (90,000) and, when a list exceeds it, raises a `RebarError`\ncarrying the new `error_code=\"response_too_large\"`. The already-installed\n`install_error_guard` converts that into the standard rebar MCP envelope, so the caller\ngets:\n\n    {\"error\": \"response_too_large\", \"message\": \"list_tickets matched 4000 tickets and\n     would return 518902 bytes, over the 90000-byte MCP response budget. No partial list\n     is returned (a short list cannot be told from a complete one). Narrow the query with\n     one of status, ticket_type, priority, parent, has_tag, without_tag -- or read a\n     single ticket with show_ticket.\", \"exit_code\": 1}\n\nDeliberately NOT the truncate-and-flag treatment a workflow payload gets: a shortened list\nis indistinguishable from a complete one, which is the vacuous-result mode this project\nrefuses. Wired into `list_tickets` AND `ready_tickets` (both named in the AC).\n\n**2. \"Lean\" is now actually lean.** `LEAN_OMITTED_FIELDS` + `lean_projection` in\n`src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py` extend the `include_body=False` drop set from\n`description`/`comments` to also drop `authorship_ledger`, `attestations`, `signature`,\n`keyring`. The snapshot backend (`_snapshot/ticket_view.py`) calls the same function, so\nthe two read backends cannot drift.\n\n### Why both halves were needed\n\n| query | before | after |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| unfiltered (2,855) | 44,392,067 | 4,928,872 |\n| per row | 15,548 | 1,726 |\n| `status=open` (51) | 224,610 | 58,867 |\n| `in_progress` (15) | 182,426 | 24,392 |\n| `tag=mcp,status=open,type=bug` (10) | 52,854 | 11,178 |\n| `ready` (61) | 693,556 | 76,878 |\n\nWithout the projection the 90 KB bound would refuse even `list_tickets(status=\"open\")`.\nWith it, every ordinary query fits and only a genuinely unbounded one is refused.\n\n### RED-first, mutation-checked\n\n`tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_list_payload_budget.py` (7 tests) was written and seen\nRED before any fix, driving the REGISTERED `CallToolRequest` handler a real client\nreaches — not just `call_tool` — so a guard applied only to the post-`build_server()`\ninstance cannot pass it.\n\nMutation check, each half reverted independently:\n\n- shrink `LEAN_OMITTED_FIELDS` back to the two body fields → **3 RED**\n  (`lean=24072 full=24156: lean is not materially smaller`)\n- neuter the budget comparison in `_bound_list_payload` → **3 RED**\n  (`an over-budget list must not come back as a result`; `DID NOT RAISE ToolError`)\n- restored → **7 GREEN**\n\n### Gates\n\n`make lint` (ruff check + format + complexity ratchet `active=39 new=0 increased=0`),\n`make typecheck` (684 files clean), `pytest tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py`\n(the extraction is what keeps `mcp_server.py` under the cap: 837 → 754),\n`tests/unit` + `tests/interfaces` — 16,375 passed after fixing the four ctx fixtures and\nregenerating `api_surface_baseline.json` for the new error code.\n\n### Still open\n\nThe **LIVE VALIDATION** criterion is NOT met and this ticket must stay open until it is:\nthe change is on Gerrit, not merged and not deployed. Evidence must be re-taken against\n`https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp` after the mcp container redeploys.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787948463256980086,"uuid":"1110a03b-a18b-4b11-947e-806779255f02"}